WEBVTT

00:00.540 --> 00:04.450
<b><b>Fire Safety</b></b>

00:02.250 --> 00:04.450
How deplorable.

00:04.960 --> 00:12.600
<i>So, they're even getting 
children like you involved.</i>

00:13.950 --> 00:15.490
What in the world?

00:15.830 --> 00:18.950
What do you mean by "Bastard 
Child of Sabaramond"?

00:19.180 --> 00:21.910
Is Sabaramond-san in this world?

00:22.170 --> 00:25.620
Do you come from the empire 
in that world, too?

00:25.870 --> 00:29.360
Or... do you have ties to 
the Kingdom of Nyanild?

00:30.650 --> 00:33.190
I don't know those terms.

00:33.690 --> 00:35.890
Is he playing dumb?

00:35.890 --> 00:39.850
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

00:35.890 --> 00:39.850
No, I don't think so.

00:40.750 --> 00:44.490
<i>Is he different from them?</i>

00:44.890 --> 00:48.100
<i>No, the same. An enemy.</i>

00:48.940 --> 00:53.610
<i>Polka Shinoyama, what are you?</i>

00:54.920 --> 00:57.450
<i>Damn it, they're not making sense!</i>

00:57.970 --> 01:01.110
<i>Those words were only just 
burned into the wall.</i>

01:01.110 --> 01:03.650
<i>Are they watching me from nearby?</i>

01:04.720 --> 01:06.730
<i>No one else is on this floor.</i>

01:07.320 --> 01:09.820
<i>Only Sayo-san is on the floor below.</i>

01:10.410 --> 01:12.250
<i>There are a few people near the building,</i>

01:13.570 --> 01:14.720
<i>and... two on the roof?</i>

01:15.560 --> 01:17.200
<i>Wait, what?</i>

01:29.950 --> 01:32.920
Not too shabby, young man!

03:07.200 --> 03:12.220
You gave me quite a fright!
You have the makings of a magician.

03:12.560 --> 03:13.630
<b>Mentally</b>

03:12.560 --> 03:13.630
<b>BA-DUMP
BA-DUMP</b>

03:12.560 --> 03:13.630
<b>BA-DUMP
BA-DUMP</b>

03:14.050 --> 03:16.590
<i>Seriously, who </i>is<i> this boy?</i>

03:16.590 --> 03:20.800
<i>For now, O goddess of fortune, at 
least let me </i>sound<i> like I have a clue!</i>

03:21.860 --> 03:23.550
Who is this guy?

03:24.010 --> 03:28.020
He's slower than the Heilei,
but his unpredictability is a pain.

03:28.660 --> 03:32.220
<i>What the hell does someone 
like him want with Polka?</i>

03:32.540 --> 03:34.530
<i>Or is he here for the fake Polka?</i>

03:35.340 --> 03:37.440
<i>Maybe I can get him to tell me.</i>

03:37.760 --> 03:40.600
So, what brings you here, mister?

03:40.600 --> 03:45.280
Are you looking for someone 
named Hosorogi, maybe?

03:46.510 --> 03:47.690
<i>Well, now.</i>

03:47.690 --> 03:50.660
<i>I don't know who that is,
but I'll take what I can get!</i>

03:50.890 --> 03:53.210
<i>Hosorogi, you're a lifesaver!</i>

03:54.420 --> 03:58.230
Oh? So, you've already guessed that much.

03:58.230 --> 03:59.760
Well, no matter.

03:59.760 --> 04:03.390
I'll repay Hosorogi some other time!

04:03.390 --> 04:08.140
<i>I did it! Good night and good luck,
goddess of fortune!</i>

04:08.140 --> 04:10.310
Repay Hosorogi?

04:10.730 --> 04:14.810
What could a wanted man like 
you owe a police IA inspector?

04:15.260 --> 04:16.190
Huh?

04:17.110 --> 04:20.860
Was that shooting a one-man show you staged?

04:21.740 --> 04:23.780
<i>Open mouth, insert foot!</i>

04:23.090 --> 04:28.080
<b>ZZZ</b>

04:23.090 --> 04:28.080
<b>ZZZ</b>

04:24.710 --> 04:27.720
<i>Wake up, goddess of fortune!</i>

04:28.080 --> 04:31.530
<i>His heartbeat sped up. Did I guess right?</i>

04:33.540 --> 04:35.900
Close... but no cigar.

04:35.900 --> 04:39.020
The shooting was a some-other-man show.

04:37.560 --> 04:39.020
<b>Half-Baked Neologism</b>

04:39.020 --> 04:42.930
However, the fact that it occurred at all

04:40.020 --> 04:50.470
<b>Struggling to keep his story straight</b>

04:42.930 --> 04:45.600
means that something happened to Hosorogi.

04:45.600 --> 04:50.690
So, out of concern, I came 
to do a little investigating.

04:50.690 --> 04:52.010
I see.

04:52.010 --> 04:55.890
<b>Hosorogi</b>

04:52.450 --> 04:55.890
<b>This Guy</b>

04:52.640 --> 04:55.470
What's his relationship
to Hosorogi?

04:52.830 --> 04:55.890
<b>Polka</b>

04:56.220 --> 04:57.360
Well, whatever.

04:58.650 --> 05:00.810
<i>Is this guy His Lordship's enemy?</i>

05:00.810 --> 05:03.360
<i>No matter what, I need to catch 
him and make him tell me!</i>

05:03.360 --> 05:06.270
Dear me, do you have another 
trick up your sleeve?

05:06.270 --> 05:10.330
Don't bother. This time,
you'll be the one in for a fright.

05:10.330 --> 05:11.310
Oh, yeah?

05:11.310 --> 05:16.670
I can't wait to see how 
you'll... surprise me!

05:30.800 --> 05:32.220
Lemmings!

05:32.680 --> 05:35.030
<i>The jack-of-all-trades turned urban legend!</i>

05:35.030 --> 05:37.450
<i>He's a monster. Identity unknown.</i>

05:37.840 --> 05:42.820
<i>And he's one of the people my family, 
the Heilei, declared off-limits.</i>

05:43.650 --> 05:46.720
Don't tell me you're working with <i>him</i>?

05:49.740 --> 05:53.270
I see you're just as shocked 
as I hoped you would be!

05:53.270 --> 05:54.900
<i>And so am I!</i>

05:54.900 --> 05:59.500
He's a dangerous fellow.
Not even I know what he'll do.

05:59.500 --> 06:01.500
<i>I really have no idea!</i>

06:01.500 --> 06:04.460
So, if you care to surrender 
and flee, now is your chance.

06:04.460 --> 06:06.170
<b>Dodging the question</b>

06:04.690 --> 06:06.170
<i>I want to run for it, too!</i>

06:06.500 --> 06:07.930
<i>I've heard of this guy!</i>

06:07.930 --> 06:08.930
<i>I don't know his name,</i>

06:08.930 --> 06:12.640
<i>but he's the master of unspecified 
employment they call Lemmings!</i>

06:12.640 --> 06:17.350
Baby-faced young man of mystery,
try not to antagonize this berserker.

06:17.350 --> 06:21.690
Once he gets started, 
not even I can stop him!

06:18.580 --> 06:21.690
<b>The unvarnished truth</b>

06:24.040 --> 06:26.610
<i>What's this? Is it curtains for me?</i>

06:28.240 --> 06:29.240
<i>You're wide open!</i>

06:33.970 --> 06:36.990
Does Rozan-sama's bodyguard 
know about Lemmings?

06:37.510 --> 06:40.830
I haven't told my family 
much about any of you.

06:41.100 --> 06:45.080
Of course, Lemmings may have been 
spotted during the recent fire.

06:46.300 --> 06:47.260
Then...

06:47.260 --> 06:51.760
Don't fret. We won't lose 
anyone to friendly fire.

06:52.010 --> 06:56.840
I warned him not to touch 
my grandfather's bodyguard.

06:57.410 --> 07:00.730
He won't go against my orders.

07:01.490 --> 07:04.470
No matter what is done to him.

07:05.870 --> 07:07.070
What the hell...

07:07.400 --> 07:09.150
What the hell is this guy?!

07:15.700 --> 07:16.870
Are you ignoring me?!

07:21.420 --> 07:22.670
I can't cut him!

07:26.500 --> 07:28.550
Then, how about this?!

07:40.840 --> 07:46.980
Th-That was your cue to grab the person 
shocking you and go out together!

07:46.980 --> 07:52.450
Today's youth is too blasé about 
electrocution! They need a wake-up call!

07:53.360 --> 07:55.410
Aren't you on the same side?!

07:56.960 --> 07:58.610
Who can say?

07:58.610 --> 08:02.390
In my eyes, the whole world 
around me is an ally.

08:02.390 --> 08:07.980
So, you could say our bandaged friend
 is on my side, and so are you!

08:07.980 --> 08:08.710
What?

08:08.710 --> 08:11.050
Say no to infighting!

08:09.610 --> 08:14.360
<b>Pretty
Please</b>

08:11.050 --> 08:14.590
Let's resolve this with 
a peaceful discussion!

08:14.590 --> 08:17.100
I've had it with your games!

08:17.100 --> 08:18.060
Enough is enough.

08:18.690 --> 08:21.060
I'll blow you both sky high!

08:21.060 --> 08:23.020
<b>Fire   Safety</b>

08:27.490 --> 08:31.240
Excuse me, miss? Do you have a moment?

08:32.350 --> 08:38.410
Oh, don't be afraid. We're with the 
Shinjuku Community Safety Division.

08:38.410 --> 08:43.120
You see, we wonder why you're wearing 
that coat in this great weather.

08:43.330 --> 08:49.840
As police officers, we can't ignore 
a kid out on the streets at 3:00 a.m.

08:49.840 --> 08:53.300
<b>Fire Safety</b>

08:53.300 --> 08:55.760
<b>Call Ended</b>

08:54.500 --> 08:55.760
<i>They hung up.</i>

08:56.080 --> 08:58.250
<i>What is it? What's going on?</i>

08:58.720 --> 09:04.190
<i>Details from my world are making it here,
although only in bits and pieces.</i>

09:04.600 --> 09:07.600
...a Bastard Child of Sabaramond?

09:08.410 --> 09:10.570
The world I ran from.

09:11.210 --> 09:15.950
<i>I've become its enemy, so corrupted 
that I can never go back,</i>

09:16.570 --> 09:19.780
<i>but it's where I remember my loved ones.</i>

09:20.450 --> 09:24.170
<i>No. Don't touch it. Don't defile it!</i>

09:31.410 --> 09:34.940
One of the people I sense 
above is definitely Lemmings.

09:35.450 --> 09:37.510
And those below seem flustered.

09:38.630 --> 09:41.250
<i>So, considering when the call ended,</i>

09:41.680 --> 09:44.680
<i>there's a good chance the caller is nearby.</i>

09:45.370 --> 09:48.810
I can't let one of my few 
clues slip through my fingers.

09:50.240 --> 09:51.240
I'll start

09:54.740 --> 09:57.610
by securing this location.

10:13.150 --> 10:15.670
Romelka? What is it?

10:16.900 --> 10:18.770
Izliz,

10:18.770 --> 10:21.220
you keep staring out to sea. 
Is something wrong?

10:21.920 --> 10:24.180
I was just waxing sentimental

10:24.740 --> 10:30.560
about a pitiful, yet refined, empire 
that fell 100 years or more ago.

10:27.700 --> 10:31.400
<b>Former Byadian Imperial Court Sorcerer, Second Rank 
"The Wandering Balcony"

 Izliz Swordflail</b>

10:27.700 --> 10:31.400
m 0 0 l 410 0 410 80 0 80

10:31.400 --> 10:34.650
Lies, lies, and more lies!

10:32.170 --> 10:37.610
<b>Same, Seventh Rank
"Roaming Woodlands"

 Romelka Remelka</b>

10:32.170 --> 10:37.610
m 0 0 l 290 0 290 80 0 80

10:34.650 --> 10:37.610
You were thinking about the 
Corpse God, weren't you?

10:37.930 --> 10:39.370
It's the same thing.

10:39.770 --> 10:45.080
Raising that dimwitted pupil was 
just about all I did for the empire.

10:45.400 --> 10:47.580
That's still an achievement to be proud of!

10:48.080 --> 10:51.970
A master and apprentice simultaneously 
being court sorcerers is almost unheard of.

10:51.970 --> 10:55.970
Even I had to wait my turn 
until my teacher retired!

10:55.970 --> 10:58.690
The Corpse God was one of the five best,

10:58.690 --> 11:02.400
and he took his necromancy in a 
different direction from yours.

11:02.400 --> 11:06.090
The way you were two sides of the 
same coin made my heart skip a beat!

11:06.090 --> 11:09.260
Or maybe sent mana rushing to my leaves.
Anyway, it was to die for!

11:09.940 --> 11:14.140
I see a century hasn't 
slowed your tongue one bit.

11:14.650 --> 11:19.510
I suppose magical longevity makes 
one proportionately slow to mature.

11:21.910 --> 11:23.600
Perhaps my fool of an apprentice

11:23.600 --> 11:26.920
remained a boy to the bitter end.

11:27.730 --> 11:30.910
What's wrong with never growing up?

11:31.190 --> 11:34.960
The Corpse God is normally such a nice boy.

11:34.960 --> 11:37.740
So different from the way he is in battle...

11:37.740 --> 11:40.200
A nice boy, is he?

11:40.840 --> 11:45.050
You have it wrong. Completely wrong.

11:45.050 --> 11:45.980
Huh?

11:45.980 --> 11:52.020
That dunce surpasses me in 
only one thing: empathy.

11:52.020 --> 11:53.550
Empathy?

11:53.550 --> 11:59.110
He never realized this himself,
but he has almost no will of his own.

11:59.480 --> 12:03.410
He gives himself over entirely 
to those he feels close to.

12:04.580 --> 12:09.660
I suppose that's why he sympathizes 
with the dead far better than I can.

12:10.130 --> 12:13.370
And that is why... that is <i>the</i> reason why...

12:14.070 --> 12:17.600
Although he doesn't mind being dragged 
through the mud one bit,

12:17.950 --> 12:20.130
when the "home" he depends on is defiled,

12:20.850 --> 12:24.010
then he... then the Corpse God...

12:25.050 --> 12:27.020
loses all control.

12:42.610 --> 12:47.280
<i>I'm supposed to watch the area around 
this building for who knows what.</i>

12:47.520 --> 12:51.790
<i>A schoolgirl in a raincoat when 
it's not raining? Kind of fishy.</i>

12:52.170 --> 12:56.400
<i>I remember the Gator Sisters, though.
I can't let my guard down because she's a girl.</i>

13:00.710 --> 13:02.670
I-I'm so sorry!

13:03.140 --> 13:08.880
You see, our dog ran away, and my 
dad and I went out looking for him.

13:08.880 --> 13:12.280
I think he went into that building.

13:12.280 --> 13:13.330
Hmm...

13:13.330 --> 13:15.340
And where's your dad now?

13:15.340 --> 13:20.920
I called to say I found Toyomaru—that's 
our dog—so he should be here soon.

13:20.920 --> 13:24.610
Oh, there he is. Dad!

13:24.610 --> 13:26.450
What do you want with my daughter?

13:26.450 --> 13:31.080
Dad, don't glare like that.
These guys are cops!

13:31.080 --> 13:35.790
Excuse me. My daughter and I 
are out looking for our dog.

13:35.790 --> 13:37.700
So, why the raincoat?

13:37.700 --> 13:41.000
So I don't get dirty searching 
nooks and crannies.

13:41.620 --> 13:45.690
<i>No. There are no living dogs near here.</i>

13:46.170 --> 13:53.370
<i>The girl speaking with the officers,
and the man facing Lemmings on the roof...</i>

13:53.370 --> 13:55.030
<i>I recognize the hues of both their souls.</i>

13:55.780 --> 14:00.020
<i>They asked me about the emblem 
when I told their fortunes.</i>

14:00.440 --> 14:01.850
<i>This is no coincidence.</i>

14:02.640 --> 14:04.580
<i>I'll expand my Temple slightly.</i>

14:13.420 --> 14:14.490
What the...?

14:15.250 --> 14:17.160
Hey, does it feel chilly to you?

14:22.350 --> 14:26.440
We'll review the basics today, boy.

14:27.210 --> 14:31.550
Starting with the construction 
of a Netherworld Overflow Temple.

14:32.500 --> 14:37.390
Have you ever felt afraid of a forest 
at night, cloaked in silence?

14:37.390 --> 14:43.030
Or experienced a sense of the sublime
 merely by standing in a shrine?

14:43.770 --> 14:49.500
By adding a hint of the other side to 
your surroundings or a closed space,

14:49.500 --> 14:54.870
you can lend them a degree of such 
invisible atmosphere at will.

14:55.350 --> 14:59.790
Those without the Evil Eye 
will merely sense the change,

14:59.790 --> 15:06.340
but with enough time, you can disorient and 
dazzle them, as you would with an illusion.

15:10.000 --> 15:12.880
Hmm... I suppose this is your limit now.

15:13.820 --> 15:16.700
Don't be in such a hurry, boy.

15:17.120 --> 15:19.530
If you keep honing your craft,

15:20.870 --> 15:24.180
you'll be able to engulf 
whole castles one day.

15:26.570 --> 15:29.860
Is it me, or did it just get a lot colder?

15:29.860 --> 15:31.030
Well now.

15:31.300 --> 15:33.490
I don't know what caused it,

15:33.490 --> 15:36.470
but something doesn't feel quite right.

15:37.660 --> 15:39.970
Lemmings is on the roof.

15:39.970 --> 15:42.770
I'd like to avoid confronting him directly.

15:43.470 --> 15:48.890
<i>Yet those who asked after the emblem are 
at the roof and the street entrance.</i>

15:49.520 --> 15:53.560
<i>If they know something, I cannot 
afford to let them escape.</i>

15:54.580 --> 15:56.960
I'll begin by assisting Xiaoyu-kun.

15:57.620 --> 15:59.850
<b>Won't people
see you?</b>

16:00.100 --> 16:02.830
Rest easy. I will use

16:04.180 --> 16:05.940
my Invisible Hands.

16:07.150 --> 16:08.240
What's going on?

16:08.870 --> 16:11.360
Something feels different all of a sudden.

16:11.780 --> 16:15.200
<i>It's like being at the bottom of a lake.</i>

16:15.600 --> 16:20.780
<i>Everything looks the same...
but I </i>know<i> something has changed.</i>

16:21.490 --> 16:25.400
<i>Hmm... Did he release some sort of gas?</i>

16:25.400 --> 16:26.130
<i>No.</i>

16:27.080 --> 16:32.760
<i>This isn't physical; it's 
merely an ominous feeling.</i>

16:32.760 --> 16:35.300
<i>It won't pay to stick around.</i>

16:38.600 --> 16:43.060
Um, excuse me, but would you mind telling me

16:43.450 --> 16:45.610
if either of you did that?

16:46.560 --> 16:47.900
Don't look at me!

16:54.460 --> 16:56.230
Wh-What the...

16:56.230 --> 16:57.570
What's going on?!

16:57.570 --> 17:01.330
You're still after me, even under 
these bizarre circumstances?!

17:02.350 --> 17:03.330
Whoops!

17:07.420 --> 17:11.130
<i>What is it? It's like something's 
been stopping us...</i>

17:11.400 --> 17:13.590
<i>The boy seems fine as far as I can see.</i>

17:13.970 --> 17:18.800
<i>Does that mean this thing is 
targeting us deliberately?</i>

17:19.480 --> 17:21.350
<i>I'm in good form.</i>

17:21.350 --> 17:25.900
<i>Sympathizing and sharing senses with 
shades is indeed far easier now.</i>

17:26.320 --> 17:32.530
<i>Fine control is simple within this Temple—
my Netherworld Overflow ward.</i>

17:32.870 --> 17:35.520
<i>So... I'll take it a step further.</i>

17:36.810 --> 17:41.130
Dear me. As fascinating as this is, 
I've seen enough for one night!

17:41.130 --> 17:43.980
Até breve, obri... something or other!

17:44.870 --> 17:48.080
Oh? It's one thing after another.

17:49.150 --> 17:49.970
Hm?

17:52.090 --> 17:55.260
As I thought, it's not much like 
an ad balloon with just me.

17:55.260 --> 17:58.970
Now hiring: extras to form a human rope!

17:57.990 --> 17:58.970
<b>Here</b>

17:58.970 --> 18:02.880
Well, I'd better call Iwa-san.

18:02.880 --> 18:06.490
Fair enough, but how much will you report?

18:06.490 --> 18:07.390
Sorry?

18:07.390 --> 18:08.850
Oh.

18:08.850 --> 18:12.070
Think <i>that's</i> another one of 
Solitaire's magic tricks?

18:13.330 --> 18:16.990
How do you like my secret smoke screen?!

18:16.990 --> 18:20.970
I added powdered cassava to recreate 
the taste of tapioca milk tea...

18:22.330 --> 18:24.160
What on earth...?

18:24.450 --> 18:28.620
<i>I wove this necromantic 
spell to suit this world.</i>

18:30.840 --> 18:31.790
It's me.

18:32.110 --> 18:35.050
<i>I'm sending video.
Please review it immediately.</i>

18:36.000 --> 18:36.970
What's happened?

18:36.970 --> 18:39.380
I'm not qualified to judge.

18:42.490 --> 18:43.550
What the...?

18:44.530 --> 18:48.260
<i>By sympathizing with the spirits of the dead,
I share senses with their hands.</i>

18:48.260 --> 18:52.930
<i>I couldn't do this well in my old world. 
Its abundant mana got in the way.</i>

18:53.670 --> 18:57.060
So, you're here, too, Fire-Breathing Bug-kun.

18:57.060 --> 19:01.010
You have some nerve,
using <i>me</i> for misdirection.

19:01.010 --> 19:02.550
But never mind! I forgive you!

19:02.550 --> 19:07.290
Why? Because I'm in a simply <i>fantastic</i> mood!

19:07.290 --> 19:14.500
Though I can't be certain, a great bridge 
of hope shines before me like a rainbow!

19:14.760 --> 19:17.960
<i>But in this mana-poor world,
it's child's play.</i>

19:17.960 --> 19:23.140
<i>And weaving in Shade Thread grants 
ghostly hands tangible force.</i>

19:23.540 --> 19:27.280
<i>I've turned this world's 
environment against it to make...</i>

19:28.440 --> 19:30.240
<i>a flock of Invisible Hands!</i>

19:34.110 --> 19:37.450
Time marches on, overturning common sense!

19:37.450 --> 19:39.030
This world is so very

19:39.410 --> 19:41.280
beautiful!

19:49.730 --> 19:52.980
<i>I see I lack the power to restrain Lemmings.</i>

19:53.460 --> 19:55.960
<i>Then I'll focus on the other one.</i>

19:56.240 --> 19:59.420
My imaginary inner child

19:59.420 --> 20:01.380
is jumping for joy!

20:01.380 --> 20:04.340
First the skeletons in the fire,
now these arms!

20:04.340 --> 20:09.310
Do they share a source? 
Do you hold the secret?

20:10.180 --> 20:14.150
I see! You are indeed true to your name!

20:14.150 --> 20:15.640
Till we meet again!

20:15.640 --> 20:20.820
I <i>will</i> uncover the truth 
about you, Corpse God!

20:24.610 --> 20:28.330
You, on the other hand,
